  "method": "Three fresh control/instrumented pairs for each of three frozen native masks. Alternate arm order. Instrumented loader records times and branches without changing forces, deadlines, masks or validity rules; overhead can change a timed trajectory. This is not a throughput comparison.",
  "findings": [
    "Half star: two of three instrumented runs reach the same step-200 proposal at 1.5580% refinement-grid error, failing only short self-clearance. Remaining phase allowance is -14.14 and -26.24 ms, so the 50 ms repair gate prevents projection. The third instrumented run stops before step 200. This verifies the missing-repair branch, not that the untried repair would succeed.",
    "Half star uses a provisional recovered routing with a 700 ms polishing phase, despite returning the full solve in roughly six seconds. Its three uninstrumented independent mask errors range from 1.7470% to 2.0801%, so the issue occurs without instrumentation.",
    "Gift: the same 4+4 initial refinement ends after 470 computed steps in every instrumented run, leaving a 5+5 alternative about 1.7-1.8 seconds. Final 4+4 polishing begins with only 0.94-0.97 seconds. This reproduces the shared allocation mechanism; all three current instrumented polishes reach the same selected error, so this run alone does not establish that capping the alternative improves quality.",
    "Warped checker: two instrumented initial refinements reach 205 steps; a slower third reaches only 125, entering polishing with 1.7319% instead of 1.5961% error. The worse final fit therefore starts before final polishing, rather than from a missed short-return repair."
  ],
  "nextExperiment": "Keep the gradient-step deadline, but allow the provisional recovery checkpoint to complete its bounded short-return projection for up to 400 ms more, capped by the existing enclosing deadline. Evaluate fresh paired fits and unchanged independent validity checks before runtime integration.",
